<title>BELGIUM: Commission rejects Danish pig aid.</title>
<headline>Commission rejects Danish pig aid.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler rejected a Danish request for private storage aid to help pig producers, an EU official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Fischler told European Union agriculture ministers on Monday that the slaughter of pigs due to swine fever would help maintain prices.</p>
<p>&quot;While the Commissioner accepted that production was predicted to rise by two to three percent in 1997, he said that swine fever was a new factor in the market,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>Fischler added that he was waiting for the outcome of talks with Japan in Geneva that took place on Monday aimed at unblocking a Japanese ban on EU pork imports.</p>
<p>&quot;He said that he would be visiting Japan in three weeks and would be raising the issue with the Japanese government,&quot; the official added.</p>
</text>
